\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"894519446970bfe90d9f6ae6e0a25131b5c2cd56432b4e4a58169534f8e32d3a","event_uuid":"9892a6fd-78f9-4944-8ac9-8e24cd228f96","position":{"commit_sha":"241b7829d0738728dfa17e79984046da4a1d5ef1","position":"1785911938149227001-9892a6fd-78f9-4944-8ac9-8e24cd228f96"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-222_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"4cf58ecd-8513-4de1-a7b6-62b672e02919","comments":[],"created_at":1785896718414675001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f06d745b-422c-47e6-8288-2888dfa450ed","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c6c9-cba0-1aa4-47eb"},{"link_uuid":"9892a6fd-78f9-4944-8ac9-8e24cd228f96","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7908-e49a-aecf-4403"},{"link_uuid":"1c38460c-b8dd-44ee-b094-e3f44ad6ad4f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"726a-51a8-87ea-49ec"}],"description":"# `plan_review/passes.py` is now at the hard cap with zero headroom\n\n## Context\n\nDiscovered while landing c6c9 (the `attest.py` split). With `attest.py` brought down to 656, the largest file in `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/` is now `passes.py` at **exactly 800** lines — the hard cap enforced by `tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py::test_no_src_module_over_the_hard_cap` (limit single-sourced in `.github/module-size-limit.txt`, gate is `> limit`).\n\nThis is the identical failure mode c6c9 was raised for: the file passes only because the comparison is strictly-greater. **Any** next edit to `passes.py` — including a one-line bug fix — cannot land without first splitting it, and that cost lands on whoever next needs to fix a bug there, under time pressure, as an unrelated blocker.\n\nCurrent top of the package (post-c6c9):\n\n    800  passes.py          <- at the cap, zero headroom\n    784  __init__.py\n    776  pass1.py\n    769  registry.py\n    759  det_floor.py\n    726  sizing.py\n    702  orchestrator.py\n\nNote this is a *cluster* problem, not a single-file one: seven files in this one package sit between 700 and 800. `passes.py` is the urgent one; the rest are a standing risk worth a broader look.\n\n## Approach\n\nSame discipline as c6c9 and 2682 — split ONLY along a seam that already exists in the call graph, never mechanically to hit a number, and never creating a sub-100-LOC file.\n\nThe c6c9 split is the worked reference for the two things that make this safe:\n\n1. **Find the reference set with BOTH tools.** Serena `find_referencing_symbols` AND a repo-wide string `grep` for each moved symbol — the LSP cannot see `monkeypatch.setattr` / `getattr` / `importlib` targets, and an empty semantic result is not trustworthy.\n2. **Watch for patch seams.** In c6c9 the moved code called two helpers that the suite monkeypatches ON the source module object; a module-level `from .x import y` in the new module would have bound the pre-patch objects and silently ignored the patches (verified: it turns 4 tests RED). Function-local imports preserve the semantics. Expect the same class of hazard here.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py` is under 700 LOC\n- [ ] any extracted module is at least 100 LOC\n- [ ] the split follows a pre-existing call-graph seam, with the caller analysis recorded in the commit message\n- [ ] zero test edits are required by the move, or each required edit is justified in the commit message\n- [ ] [operator-attested] the full suite passes with a test count equal to the pre-split count, evidenced by the two pytest summary lines quoted in a comment","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","726a-51a8-87ea-49ec"],["relates_to","7908-e49a-aecf-4403"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"293d591b-1392-43e5-88fd-9f75a2215610","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8705-5c65-c1b6-42de","ticket_type":"task","title":"passes.py sits at exactly 800/800 LOC — the next file at the cap","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f13c678d-c679-4f7c-8c00-9d3542574c51","f06d745b-422c-47e6-8288-2888dfa450ed","a28fc37e-425c-41d9-9f1d-9f5abd1643dc","293d591b-1392-43e5-88fd-9f75a2215610","0d0d6fd8-8028-49b7-8bd0-7142dd474a07","9892a6fd-78f9-4944-8ac9-8e24cd228f96","1c38460c-b8dd-44ee-b094-e3f44ad6ad4f"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785916792128274116,"uuid":"3344de4a-f7b2-430a-aca4-5c8adf1def70"}